in @prism
in @glass
in @meta
in @spectral
in @spectral/supervisor
in @loop
in @epistemologic/reality/time

# @spectral/restart_intensity — the supervisor's storm-protection
# carrier. Substrate-decl form of BEAM's max_restarts / max_seconds
# circuit breaker.
#
# Closes the forward-promise at `shards/spectral/supervisor.mirror`
# line ~253: `restart_intensity.mirror` was named as a cascade sibling
# but deferred pending the math floor. The math landed at
# `docs/math/supervisor/emergent-supervision-from-geometry.md` §5
# (Mara `a3dec7b`, Seam-ratified `3746197`). This shard is the
# substrate-decl form the §5.5 template collapses to.
#
# Operationalizes candidate recognition #147 (renumbered at `ff00ec5`
# from the original #136 per Reed's numbering-collision resolution):
# restart-intensity IS a `@spawn ≤ @loop` instance at supervision
# altitude. The math floor: §5.3 (composition) + §5.4 (Rice-safety
# via budget-as-witness) + §5.5 (this shard's template).
#
# === What restart_intensity IS ===
#
# The typed carrier the supervisor's `child_spec` will surface to
# gate the kintsugi-morphism-driven restart loop. Two fields:
#
#   budget — the initial restart allowance B₀. Monotone descent per
#            `docs/math/spawn/spawn-as-loop-monad.md` §3.1: each
#            `bind` step (each restart attempt) decrements by 1;
#            `terminal_check` fires when budget = 0. Typed `ref` per
#            [[feedback-no-bare-types]] + [[feedback-explicit-over-
#            implicit]] (Alex 2026-07-02): bare `u32`/`u64` would let
#            same-shape different-meaning integers flow through the
#            type system, indistinguishable from an unrelated count.
#            The `ref` carrier composes with `@spawn ≤ @loop`'s
#            `budget: ref` field (Mara `7dba128` §3.1) at supervision
#            altitude — same carrier, same discipline, same halting
#            witness (per §5.4).
#
#   period — the time window within which the budget applies.
#            Reuses the substrate's landed `duration` carrier from
#            `@epistemologic/reality/time` (`type duration = settle({
#            nanos: u64 })`; commit c8c88f2). Composes with
#            `child_spec.shutdown: duration` at the supervisor
#            altitude — one substrate-time carrier for both
#            graceful-termination and storm-protection windows.
#
# === Recognition ancestry ===
#
# - Candidate #147 (this arc; substrate-pull-supervisor-emergence):
#   supervision-altitude primitives are declaration ceremonies over
#   substrate carriers already in place. Restart intensity is one row
#   of the emergence table (`docs/math/supervisor/emergent-
#   supervision-from-geometry.md` §1.1, row 5).
# - Recognition #53 (property/fracture bilateral pattern; promoted):
#   this shard is NOT a bilateral instance itself — it is the CARRIER
#   that a future bilateral pair (`@epistemologic/property/
#   restart_intensity_well_formed` + `@kintsugi/fracture/
#   restart_storm`; supervisor forward-promise line 269-272) will
#   predicate on. Bilaterals need something to be bilateral ABOUT.
#   Craft discipline: land the carrier first; the bilateral is a
#   separate cascade tick at pact + kintsugi altitude.
# - [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]: grep 2026-07-03
#   confirmed `restart_intensity`, `max_restarts`, `max_seconds` are
#   NOT already declared in the substrate (only `restart_kind` +
#   `restart_strategy` at `@spectral/supervisor`). This tick lands a
#   genuinely new carrier; no substrate-collapse available.
# - [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]]: substrate source IS
#   substrate data; this shard IS the declaration.
#
# === Composition with `@spawn ≤ @loop` ===
#
# `@spawn ≤ @loop` (Mara `7dba128`; math at `docs/math/spawn/spawn-
# as-loop-monad.md` §3.1) landed `budget: ref` as the halting witness
# for spawn-shaped bounded loops. The parent abstraction: any spawn
# whose bind-count is bounded IS a `@loop` with a monotone-descending
# budget. `restart_intensity` specializes that parent at SUPERVISION
# altitude: BEAM's max_restarts IS the initial B₀; BEAM's max_seconds
# IS the substrate-time predicate on the loop's tick_history
# (per §5.3, steps 1-5). One primitive, two altitudes; no separate
# circuit-breaker mechanism needed at supervision.
#
# === Prior art ===
#
# BEAM's supervisor `max_restarts / max_seconds` fields (OTP
# `supervisor` behaviour, since Erlang/OTP R6 — Armstrong 1996,
# *Making reliable distributed systems in the presence of software
# errors*, PhD thesis Ch. 4 §4.3.3). The circuit-breaker discipline
# prevents unbounded restart loops when a permanent-restart child
# has a deterministic startup failure: N restarts in T seconds →
# escalate to the supervisor's own parent (per §5.4 escalation-by-
# monotone-descent).
#
# === DEFERRED per [[feedback-composition-claims-need-empirical-test]] ===
#
# Whether `(budget, period)` empirically captures BEAM's
# `{max_restarts, max_seconds}` semantics under a REAL restart storm
# is unwitnessed at this tick. Per §5.5 H4 flag: two-tick empirical
# validation required — (a) deterministic-failure child with
# `budget = 3`; observe budget descent + escalation; (b) intermittent-
# failure child with `budget = 3, period = 5s`; observe budget refresh
# at period boundary. This shard lands the CARRIER; the empirical
# witness lands at Alex's altitude when a runtime supervisor exercises
# the storm-protection loop.
#
# Seam DEFER note (audit `3746197`) also flagged this: composition
# claim at supervision altitude is analytical, not yet empirical.
# Landing the carrier is Rice-safe (the carrier makes no runtime
# promise); the empirical claim stays DEFERRED.

glass @spectral/restart_intensity {
  focus restart_intensity
  project restart_intensity
  split restart_intensity
  shift restart_intensity
  settle restart_intensity
}

# === restart_intensity — the storm-protection carrier ===
#
# Two-field record. `budget: ref` is the monotone-descent witness;
# `period: duration` is the time window. Identity contract: byte-
# equality on the (budget, period) tuple.
type restart_intensity = {
  budget: ref,
  period: duration,
}

out @spectral/restart_intensity
out restart_intensity
